  "notes": ["Both source and target use narrowed original normal Sasuke queues and declared rigid poses. The source always has a role-08 sphere. The target has only the ordinary capsule except in the both-corrected control.","The original stage solver generates the vectors. The host declares only the reciprocal actor masks and target +204 scalar, not the corrections or the source of a live link.","An isolated fork captures original stage output and the propagation writer call. The enclosing original collision walk reproduces the final roots, vectors and capsule centers, with presentation not entered.","The target can receive the correction only with all four declared bits in these probes. Clearing any bit, reaching the exclusive scalar threshold, or already having its own wall correction prevents transfer.","The transferred vector moves the target capsule's broad center; allocated endpoints do not move. The matched Tau probe without transfer misses, while the transferred target reaches the kernel with shifted scratch endpoints and loses 17 HP under token 1. The source body loses no HP.","This does not establish which retail actions create or maintain the masks, live link lifetime, multi-actor chains, hardware or a native gameplay rule."],
